body:
Nice, this is very close to the implementation path I was looking at as well. Since you already have the Z-error aggregation and OperationRepresentation mapping underway, I’ll avoid duplicating that work.

I can instead look into the validation/benchmarking side: comparing the aggregated path against the current PEC implementation under fixed seeds, measuring the reduction in QPD norm / required samples, and checking estimator equivalence on small circuits. I’d also be interested in exploring how the abstraction could generalize beyond the Z-only case once the initial API settles.

@anishbhujbal7, if there are particular benchmark cases or tests that would be useful for your prototype, feel free to ping me. @MathysRennela, happy to take another slice instead if there’s something you think would be more useful.
